---
title: Neapolitan pizza dough
servings: 6
yield: 6%balls
tags: [italian, pizza, basics]
source: https://github.com/cooklang/cookcli
description: A slow dough that rewards patience. Make it the morning of the day you bake.
---

Pour the @water{533%ml} into a #large bowl{} and dissolve the @salt{24.6%g} in it. Stir in @tipo 00 flour{80%g} so that the yeast never meets the salt directly.

> The first spoonfuls of flour act as a buffer between the yeast and the salt.

Crumble in the @fresh yeast{1.6%g} and stir until it has dissolved, then add the remaining @tipo 00 flour{760%g} and mix with one hand until no dry flour is left.

Knead in the bowl for a few minutes, then turn the dough out onto a lightly floured surface and knead for ~{10-20%minutes}, until smooth and elastic. It may feel dry at first; keep going and it comes together. Shape it into one ball.

Rub a clean bowl with a little @olive oil{}, put the dough in, brush the top with oil and cover. Rest for ~{2%hours} at room temperature.

Divide into six pieces of about 230 g each, shape each into a tight ball, set them on a #baking tray{} and cover. Let them rise for ~{4-6%hours} at room temperature before stretching.
